# IGNITOR — FE I / FE II 2026–27 Syllabus Renewal Cascade

> Author: Rubén Vega Balbás, PhD (with Claude) · Ignited 2026-08-08
> Prerequisite reading: [`../2026-27-syllabus-renewal-plan.md`](../2026-27-syllabus-renewal-plan.md) (the rationale — why every decision below was made) and [`../profield-frontend-pedagogy.md`](../profield-frontend-pedagogy.md) (the research grounding, GAP/NOISE-triaged). This file and the phase files below are the **executable** layer built from that rationale; they assume you've read it, they don't repeat it.

## What this is

A **cascade**: six phases, each with an `Entry` condition, a `Do` (the actual task), and a `Gate` (the explicit test that must pass before the next phase starts). Each `phase-N-*.md` file in this directory is self-contained enough to hand to a fresh agent session as its task brief — it re-states the context it needs rather than assuming conversation history.

**To execute a phase:** open `phase-N-*.md`, treat its "Do" section as the task, its "Entry" as the precondition to verify first, its "Gate" as the done-criteria to check before reporting the phase complete and moving to `phase-(N+1)`.

## Operating rules (apply to every phase, not restated in each file)

1. **Definition of done = a published web endpoint, not a committed file** — in the long run. For phases run in *this* session (confirmed with Rubén, 2026-08-08): he pushes, the agent doesn't (see rule 9). So the per-phase checkpoint here is *content complete, committed locally, and verified with a local Jekyll build* (`bundle exec jekyll build` inside `web-foundations/`, or the repo's existing local-serve script — check `web-foundations/scripts/` and `package.json` first rather than assuming the command) producing the correct `_site/` path for each `permalink:`. Treat "file written," "local build verified," and "actually live" as three different checkboxes — this session only closes the first two per phase; the third happens on Rubén's own schedule after he reviews and pushes.
2. **Tracks sequence canonical lessons; they never duplicate lesson content inline.** `/tracks/fei/` and `/tracks/feii/` are index-and-sequence pages over `web-foundations/docs/lessons/en|es/*`. New FE II content is authored as lessons under `docs/lessons/`, then linked from the track index — never written only inside the track page.
2a. **A track's session sequence is declared in `web-foundations/docs/_data/tracks.yml`**, not invented per-phase. This file already has a schema — two tracks (`ilustracion-webapp`, `geo-physical-aggregator`), each with `sessions_list` (`title`/`slug`/`description`/`duration`/`tags` per session), `objectives`, `deliverables`, `methodology`, `evaluation`. Add `fei:` and `feii:` entries using the same schema; don't invent a parallel structure. Note: FE I semester 2 already has an equivalent hand-authored sequence at `docs/lessons/en/react/index.md` (15 lessons, 4 phases, durations, dependency graph, assessment weights) that predates this schema and isn't yet mirrored into `tracks.yml` — Phase 1 reconciles the two rather than picking one arbitrarily. FE I semester 1 (vanilla) has **no** such sequence anywhere yet — only the unordered lesson-browser grid at `/lessons/en/` (`_data/lessons.yml`) — Phase 1 has to build this ordering, not just relabel it.
2b. **Prácticas de Laboratorio must be explicitly allocated, not left blended into a single per-lesson duration.** The official guide splits hours into distinct categories — Lección Magistral 10h / Prácticas de Laboratorio 30h / Resolución de Ejercicios 14h / Estudio autónomo 94h / Evaluación 2h (150h total, both courses). Neither `react/index.md` nor `tracks.yml`'s existing tracks separate these — each session has one blended `duration`. For FE I (Phase 1, retrofitting) and FE II (Phase 2, from the start), each session in `tracks.yml`'s `sessions_list` needs a `labHours` (or equivalent) figure alongside `duration`, summing to 30h per course — this is what Phase 5 actually needs to fill in the official `ACTIVIDADES FORMATIVAS` table truthfully, not just cite the aggregate 10/30/14/94/2 figure without knowing which session contributes which hours.
3. **Exact URLs, set via Jekyll `permalink:` frontmatter** (folder nesting is free, the permalink is what matters — same pattern already used by `tracks/es/ilustracion-webapp/index.md` and `evaluation/en/index.md`):
   - FE I track index → `/tracks/fei/`
   - FE I how-to-pass-this-track → `/tracks/fei/how-to-pass-this-track/`
   - FE II track index → `/tracks/feii/`
   - FE II how-to-pass-this-track → `/tracks/feii/how-to-pass-this-track/`
4. **Any reveal.js build keeps data, code, and design tokens in separate files** — modeled on the working precedent at `/Users/ruvebal/src/MSCA/SVCM/web/pitch/` (`index.html` structure-only, `data/content.json` for slide text, `design/tokens.json` for palette, `vendor/reveal.js`+`reveal.css` vendored locally, no build step, `site.css`'s existing CSS custom properties reused rather than a second token system invented). Never inline slide content or hex colors directly into `index.html`.
5. **GAP vs. NOISE discipline when citing `profield-frontend-pedagogy.md`:** a `[UNVERIFIED-GAP]` claim is a legitimate design brief, safe to build a unit around. A `[UNVERIFIED-NOISE]` claim (there is exactly one in that document — the "skill half-life" formal-construct claim) is excluded from design reasoning entirely.
6. **`how-to-pass-this-track.md`** (in the parent directory) is the shared institutional source of truth (UDIT's literal submission template) and methodology reference — it is not itself published. The two live pages (`/tracks/fei/how-to-pass-this-track/`, `/tracks/feii/how-to-pass-this-track/`) are each instantiated from it with track-specific weights/dates/deliverables, not copied verbatim.
7. **Don't cite the Back-End II scope or the Data-Science cross-listing as if independently documented.** Both facts rest on Rubén's direct professor contact and first-hand knowledge — the full-degree syllabi JSONs that would otherwise verify them (`1500203`, `1500206` in `/Users/ruvebal/src/unicrawler/output/udit-syllabi/`) are empty stubs (`subject_count: 0`). Fine as a basis for the synergy sheet (Phase 5); don't present it as documentary fact in the TEMARIO submission.

8. **Every track index (`/tracks/fei/`, `/tracks/feii/`) opens with a short pedagogy/mission section, not just a syllabus table.** **Settled 2026-08-10: the tagline is exactly _"Critical coding for a better living."_ — never extended.** An earlier pass shipped *"…for all humans and machines"* on both track pages and in unit 12; Rubén reverted it. Use the tagline verbatim, and never write prose that quotes half of it — express the idea in your own words so the sentence survives a wording correction. Structure it like the `ilustracion-webapp` precedent (mission framing + AI-disclosure statement, right after the TOC, before the track body) but with original wording drawn from what's already grounded in `../profield-frontend-pedagogy.md`/`../frontend-pedagogy.yaml`: front-end as the human-facing interaction layer (not website production), the durable-core/volatile-layer split, the docs-first/disclosed/verified AI stance, and accessibility as an ethical practice, not a checklist. The "for machines" half of Rubén's framing has one direct existing hook — `human-machine interface pedagogy` is already a keyword in `frontend-pedagogy.yaml` — extend it toward performance/accessibility engineering as consideration for the systems code runs on and the people/assistive tech reading it, not just literal "website production." This is new interpretive writing, not a lookup — flag it back to Rubén for a pass rather than treating it as settled. This elevates pedagogy from Phase 4's CV-only blurb to something students actually see; Phase 4's CV section still happens, but is no longer the only place this shows up.

9. **The agent does not run `git push` in this session.** Confirmed with Rubén (2026-08-08): he pushes, on his own schedule, once he's reviewed a phase's diff — this is also why rule 1's Gate criteria are softened to "committed + locally build-verified" rather than "live." The agent may commit locally at each phase boundary (reversible, stays local, gives Rubén a clean diff to review) but stops there.

10. **All internal links in new content use the site's existing relative-URL convention — never a hardcoded `https://ruvebal.github.io/web-atelier-udit/...` string.** Confirmed with Rubén (2026-08-08): follow the pattern already used in `tracks/es/ilustracion-webapp/index.md` and every `_layouts/*.html` file — `{{ '/path/' | relative_url }}` in Markdown/Liquid content (resolves through `baseurl: /web-atelier-udit` correctly wherever the site is served from), or a relative `./slug/` link between sibling files in the same lesson folder, matching `docs/lessons/en/react/index.md`'s own convention. This applies to `tracks.yml`-driven track indexes, lesson cross-references, and the how-to-pass-this-track pages alike.

